.policy "ruff-n816-mixed-case-variable-in-global-scope" revision 2
.description "Name module-level variables in lowercase snake_case, not mixedCase, as PEP 8 recommends for variable names."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff N816 (pep8-naming): a name stored at module level in mixedCase: not all lowercase, and its first letter
// (after one `_`) lowercase. Exempt: namedtuple/NamedTuple assignments and names matching
// `pep8-naming.ignore-names`. A `global` statement does not make a function's store module-level here: Ruff
// checks the scope the store is written in.
//   myVariable = 0                    ← N816
//   MyObj = namedtuple("MyObj", ["a"])   not reported (and not mixedCase)
#include "python/naming.rr"

.violation N816(at: node, x: symbol) code "N816"
    "Rename `{x}` to lowercase snake_case, such as `my_variable`, and update its uses; keep the name if other modules import it or it mirrors an external API."
    suppress ruff "N816"
N816(n, x) :- store_name(n, x, m), kind(m, "module"), mixed_name(x), !store_makes(n, "namedtuple"), !naming_ignored(x).
